{{!-- The attribute row both actor headers draw: three rollable caps with steppers, HP with
      steppers, Armor read-only. The steppers write the CURRENT value, and only on a sheet the user
      may write — an observer reads the numbers and rolls the saves, and the number then sits
      centred in its cell as Armor's always does.

      @param abilities  [{key, value, max}]
      @param system     the actor's system — HP and the summed Armor
      @param seed       ink seed prefix, so each sheet's brush marks keep their own silhouette
      @param editable   @root.editable — the steppers are drawn only then --}}
{{!-- Five brush caps, and nothing under them. Each used to sit over a drawn rule; five short
      segments across the top of the sheet marked no boundary the caps were not already
      marking, and read as clutter. The cap says where a column begins and the gap says where
      it ends.

      Every number in this row is a printed LABEL and nothing else — no action, no tab stop,
      no tooltip, no text cursor, and `pointer-events: none` so a drag across the sheet cannot
      even select it. It used to be an input styled until it stopped looking like one, then a
      span that swapped a borderless field in on click; both are gone. A value on the sheet
      face is read, and it is written in exactly two places: the steppers beside it, and the
      edit window behind the quill.

      That is the rule the maximum has always followed, and the current value now follows it
      too. Two ways to type the same number into the same document, a click apart, is two
      places to keep a clamp, a commit and a re-render in step — and the sheet face is the
      worse of the two, because it is the one being read at the table.

      The two steppers either side change the CURRENT value by one, clamped to 0 and the
      maximum. They are always in the row, so nothing moves when one is reached for or runs
      out of range; a hold repeats, and the writes are coalesced in `_steppers.js`. The plus sits
      past the maximum rather than between the two numbers, where "11 + /13" read as an
      expression. --}}
<div class="cairn-attributes">
    {{#each abilities as |ability|}}
    {{!-- The three attribute caps are rolls, and they say so: hovering one re-inks the brush
          mark in blood red and brightens the word (`data-ink-lift="blood"`, painted in
          `module/ink.js`; `.is-rollable` in the stylesheet). Deepening the black mark was the
          first attempt and it was too quiet to read as an affordance at all — at this size a
          third more ink on an already near-black mark is a change nobody sees.

          The colour is drawn rather than styled for the same reason everything else here is:
          the mark is a ragged brush silhouette, and a CSS background would put a rectangle
          behind it. HP and ARMOR below are plain labels and get none of it — the difference
          IS the affordance. The link keeps the keyboard's focus ring for the same reason. --}}
    <div class="cairn-stat">
        <div class="cairn-cap is-rollable" data-ink-lift="blood">
            <span class="cairn-slab" data-ink="slab" data-ink-seed="{{../seed}}-{{ability.key}}"></span>
            <a data-action="rollSave" data-ability="{{ability.key}}" tabindex="0"
                data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.Save' key=ability.key}}">{{localize ability.key}}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="cairn-stat-value">
            {{#if ../editable}}<a class="cairn-step" data-action="statStep" data-step="-1" data-field="system.abilities.{{ability.key}}.value">&minus;</a>{{/if}}
            <span class="cairn-stat-number">
                {{!-- `data-field` and `data-max` are not an affordance: `_steppers.js#markStepLimits`
                      reads them to decide which of the two steppers has run out of range. --}}
                <span class="cairn-stat-current"
                    data-field="system.abilities.{{ability.key}}.value"
                    data-max="{{ability.max}}">{{ability.value}}</span>
                <span class="cairn-stat-max">/{{ability.max}}</span>
            </span>
            {{#if ../editable}}<a class="cairn-step" data-action="statStep" data-step="1" data-field="system.abilities.{{ability.key}}.value">+</a>{{/if}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/each}}

    <div class="cairn-stat">
        <div class="cairn-cap">
            <span class="cairn-slab" data-ink="slab" data-ink-seed="{{seed}}-hp"></span>
            <span>{{localize 'CAIRN.HitProtection'}}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cairn-stat-value">
            {{#if editable}}<a class="cairn-step" data-action="statStep" data-step="-1" data-field="system.hp.value">&minus;</a>{{/if}}
            <span class="cairn-stat-number">
                <span class="cairn-stat-current"
                    data-field="system.hp.value"
                    data-max="{{system.hp.max}}">{{system.hp.value}}</span>
                <span class="cairn-stat-max">/{{system.hp.max}}</span>
            </span>
            {{#if editable}}<a class="cairn-step" data-action="statStep" data-step="1" data-field="system.hp.value">+</a>{{/if}}
        </div>
    </div>

    {{!-- Armor is summed from equipped items and capped at 3 by rule, so it has no field
          anywhere and no steppers either — there is nothing here a player could correctly
          set by hand. --}}
    <div class="cairn-stat">
        <div class="cairn-cap">
            <span class="cairn-slab" data-ink="slab" data-ink-seed="{{seed}}-armor"></span>
            <span>{{localize 'CAIRN.Armor'}}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cairn-stat-value">
            <span class="cairn-stat-number"><span class="cairn-stat-current">{{system.armorTotal}}</span></span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
